id: pm-web-s2zw
title: List pm-lint and pm-review in the package catalog and fail on catalog drift
description: "The package catalog is the single source of truth for the per-project Packages view but omits two public fleet packages: pm-lint (authoring-quality lint rules, capabilities commands+schema) and pm-review (bot review findings as durable tracker items, capabilities commands+schema). Both are release-gated and absent from npm, so they must be catalogued as availability \"unreleased\" exactly as pm-ado and pm-jev are, with the real command lists and honest credential metadata. Also add an explicit drift test: the catalog must contain every public unbraind/pm-* repository named in a checked-in fixture list, so a new fleet package can never be silently missing again."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-14T04:44:35.979Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-14T15:26:11.384Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-14T15:26:11.377Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-14T15:26:11.377Z"
author: pi-agent
resolution: Implemented and merged in #197 (06958bd).
expected_result: The change described by this item is on main.
actual_result: "Merged in #197 as 06958bd; checks successful at head 319bfbf: CodeQL, codeql, test (22), test (26)."
comments[15]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-14T04:44:58.261Z",pi-agent,"Plan: (1) add catalog entries for pm-lint (commands: pm lint, pm lint rules; capabilities commands+schema from its manifest) and pm-review (commands: pm review import/verdict/round/precedents; capabilities commands+schema), both availability \"unreleased\" like pm-ado, descriptions mirrored verbatim from each manifest on origin/main, pm-review declaring the GitHub token it reads (GITHUB_TOKEN, then GH_TOKEN, then the gh CLI) as its import/round credentials. (2) regenerate the committed fleet snapshot so the existing snapshot-based completeness and availability gates cover both packages (they ship manifest.json with capabilities, so the live-fleet freshness gate would otherwise fail). (3) add an explicit checked-in fixture list of every public unbraind/pm-* repository (pm-ado .. pm-web, minus pm-cli and the pm-web host) and a drift test asserting the catalog contains every fixture name, with a cross-check that the fixture cannot go stale against the regenerated snapshot."
  "2026-10-14T04:47:31.031Z",pi-agent,"Regenerating the committed fleet snapshot (the gate's freshness assertion re-derives it from the fleet checkouts, which are clean on main) added pm-lint and pm-review as expected, and also surfaced a pre-existing drift the stale snapshot had hidden: pm-brief's manifest now declares capabilities [commands, schema, services] (dropped renderers, gained services) and its command list grew to nine commands (brief, brief prompt, brief next, brief stale, brief momentum, brief since, brief diverge, brief duplicates, brief governance). Fixing the pm-brief entry in the same change, because the snapshot-based capability mirror gate fails otherwise and the catalog's truthfulness contract requires mirroring the real manifest."
  "2026-10-14T04:51:31.599Z",pi-agent,"Behavioural revert proof (catalog suite, standalone mode, no fleet env needed for the failing assertion): with only the pm-review catalog entry removed, the drift test fails with \"these public unbraind/pm-* repositories are in the fixture list but absent from the catalog ... pm-review\" plus the snapshot completeness gate; with only the pm-lint entry removed, the same drift test fails naming pm-lint. Both entries restored; catalog suite green afterwards (21/21 with the fleet env var pointed at the fleet checkouts)."
  "2026-10-14T04:53:24.489Z",pi-agent,"Test note: the first linked command variant (no fleet env var) fails in this environment only because the package worktree sits in a shared worktree farm where sibling worktrees of other fleet repos are picked up as the implicit fleet root, so the live-fleet freshness gate compares them against the committed snapshot. In a standalone CI checkout the same derivation finds no siblings and skips, which is the environment that guards the merge; the fleet-root variant (command 2/2) passes 21/21 with the live-fleet gates fully active. This is an environment-sensitivity gap in the implicit fleet-root default, not a catalog defect; reported to the orchestrator in the final summary rather than changed here."
  "2026-10-14T07:03:39.289Z",pi-agent,"Gates on the final state: npm release:check and bun release:check both passed 577/577 under the isolated identity (fresh HOME, no global git config), with the fleet root resolved so the live-fleet gates ran fully active; changelog:full and changelog:check both pass (this item enters the changelog when the orchestrator closes it after verification, matching the existing Unreleased-section pattern). The three intermittent failures seen during retries (catalog install acceptance spawn ENOTDIR / 300s timeout, and the 2000-item graph read over 10s) are the documented environment-load flakes tracked in pm-web-qdhx, pm-web-fhob and pm-web-hqqp; each passed on the very next run and clean main shows the same sensitivity."
  "2026-10-14T09:16:36.322Z",pi-agent,"PR #197 CodeRabbit round 1: both Minor findings verified against pm-review origin/main commands.ts and README. Registered commands are find, import, verdict, round and precedents; only find is absent. GitHub authentication is optional for the package and required for import, round and verdict --apply. Plan: correct both catalog fields, add independent regression assertions, regenerate the documented snapshot and verify the hand-maintained roster, rebuild dist, prove each assertion fails with its catalog field reverted, then run isolated npm and Bun release gates. Branch contains current origin/main after fast-forward pull."
  "2026-10-14T09:17:31.185Z",pi-agent,"Both targeted regression assertions fail behaviourally when only their corresponding catalog fields are reverted: removing pm review find gives 0/1 pass with the missing-command deep-equality AssertionError; removing optional: true gives 0/1 pass with undefined versus true. Each experiment loads and runs normally, with zero skips; source bytes restored after each. Built server and frontend regenerated. The public package roster is deliberately hand-maintained and already includes pm-lint and pm-review; snapshot regeneration is running through npm run fleet:snapshot."
  "2026-10-14T09:18:29.023Z",pi-agent,"Restored focused acceptance via pm test --run --only-last --progress passed 23/23, zero failures, skips, cancellations or todo, including both new regressions and real scratch-tracker built acceptance. Snapshot generator rewrote the 23-extension registry receipt byte-for-byte; the 24-entry independent public roster and snapshot cross-check pass unchanged. npm ci, server/frontend build, test compilation, changelog:full and changelog:check pass. Full npm release gate now running with PM_PATH and PM_AUTHOR unset, fresh HOME, and global/system Git identity disabled; live fleet checks enabled."
  "2026-10-14T09:32:07.702Z",pi-agent,"First isolated npm release:check failed: 579 tests, 577 pass, 1 fail, 1 canceled, zero skipped/todo. Built catalog-install acceptance reached its unchanged 300-second deadline; source acceptance failed scratch-lock cleanup with ENOTEMPTY. Coverage consequently failed statements/lines at 89.70% against 90%; branches 80.21% and functions 93.09%. Both new catalog regressions and live-fleet checks passed. Preserving this failed receipt; one unchanged full npm retry started. Catalog-install timing/cleanup remains an existing host-load risk; no assertions, thresholds or production logic changed."
  "2026-10-14T09:48:35.938Z",pi-agent,"The one unchanged npm retry also failed: 579 tests, 577 pass, 1 fail, 1 canceled, zero skipped/todo. Built catalog installation timed out at 300 seconds; source catalog initial listing reported spawn ENOTDIR. Statements/lines 89.68%, branches 80.15%, functions 93.09%, so the 90% statement/line thresholds remain unmet on this failed run. Both targeted regressions passed again. Existing host-load risks pm-web-qdhx and pm-web-fhob remain open; no duplicate item created. Required isolated Bun release:check now running; no further npm retry."
  "2026-10-14T10:10:54.501Z",pi-agent,"First isolated Bun release:check failed only on the source catalog-install 300-second timeout: 579 tests, 578 pass, 0 fail, 1 canceled, zero skips/todo. Built installation acceptance passed in 262777 ms. Coverage met unchanged thresholds: statements/lines 90.64%, branches 80.66%, functions 93.45%, but the canceled test makes the gate fail and prevents downstream release checks from running. One unchanged full Bun retry started; both catalog metadata regressions passed."
  "2026-10-14T10:34:32.113Z",pi-agent,"Bun retry passed 579/579, zero fail/cancel/skip/todo; coverage statements/lines 90.58%, branches 80.55%, functions 93.45%. Production audit clean and all four packed current/minimum npm/Bun scenarios pass. Full gate then failed changelog:check because shared origin/main advanced to the version-only 2026.10.14 release commit during these long runs. Regenerated changelog via changelog:full. Recording this split result honestly, committing the reviewed fix, then merging the newer origin/main release commit and running the required gates on the resulting branch; no bot replies or manual triggers."
  "2026-10-14T10:59:23.575Z",pi-agent,"After merging the version-only main release commit, isolated npm run release:check PASS on the merged candidate: 579/579, zero failures/cancellations/skips/todo; statements/lines 90.64%, branches 80.63%, functions 93.45% at unchanged thresholds. Typechecks, lint, zero duplication, docstrings, zero production audit findings, package dry-run, all four packed npm/Bun current/minimum scenarios, changelog, version-derived release dates and publish attestation pass. Earlier failed attempts remain recorded. Starting the required Bun gate on the same source/build inputs."
  "2026-10-14T11:13:32.306Z",pi-agent,"First Bun gate on the merged 2026.10.14 candidate failed with the existing installation pattern: 579 tests, 577 pass, 1 fail, 1 canceled, zero skips/todo. Built catalog acceptance timed out at 300 seconds and source initial listing failed; coverage statements/lines 89.68%, branches 80.16%, functions 93.09%. Npm full release gate on this same merged code is already PASS 579/579 including all downstream checks. Both new metadata regressions pass under Bun. Starting one unchanged Bun retry for the merged candidate, preserving the failed receipt."
  "2026-10-14T11:42:16.906Z",pi-agent,"Final merged candidate gates PASS: npm run release:check 579/579 (statements/lines 90.64%, branches 80.63%, functions 93.45%); bun run release:check on its one unchanged retry 579/579 (90.60%, 80.61%, 93.45%). Both have zero fail/cancel/skip/todo, unchanged thresholds, zero duplication, documented declarations, zero production audit findings, four packed current/minimum npm/Bun scenarios, changelog/date and publish-attestation checks passing. Both ran with PM_PATH and PM_AUTHOR unset, fresh HOME, GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null, GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 and PM_FLEET_ROOT configured for the fleet. Known catalog-install timeout/spawn ENOTDIR flakes remain open under existing follow-up context; failed attempts are preserved above. Findings verified against pm-review main 7ac4a21: add find to the complete five-command list and mark GitHub credentials optional, naming import/round/verdict --apply. Both independent regressions pass and each fails with only its own field reverted. Implementation commit 82c5f9c; main release merge 039e18c. Releasing the claim without closing this item for orchestrator verification."
